    {
      "id": "canon-standard-section-3",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "2. One shape",
      "position": {
        "x": 810,
        "y": -260
      },
      "width": 620,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "2. One shape",
        "body": "The Detail defines the graph's shape, and the views behind it take it. Each view's own size says when it appears: the Summary is smaller than the Detail and appears sooner.\n\n*Why:* Views that share a shape look the same in a workspace tile, a portal and the graph itself, whatever the zoom.\n\n*Checked by:* faceShapeIssues (mechanical).",
