    {
      "id": "canon-standard-section-4",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "3. Derived, not typed",
      "position": {
        "x": 1530,
        "y": -260
      },
      "width": 620,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "3. Derived, not typed",
        "body": "The Detail, the Summary and the Glyph are written by the template's own Method, which a graph.changed event runs through an invokes edge. There is no stored summary node and no copy that is kept in step by hand. The saved file holds the current views.\n\n*Why:* A summary that is typed goes stale, and a stale one is worse than none.\n\n*Checked by:* Test: the stored views equal what the Method derives (mechanical).",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "canon-standard"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
