    {
      "id": "canon-standard-section-8",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "7. Pieces are classes, and relationships have names",
      "position": {
        "x": 90,
        "y": 220
      },
      "width": 620,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "7. Pieces are classes, and relationships have names",
        "body": "Each kind of thing in the template is a node class, imported through a Bridge, and each node carries the class's ports. Relationships are edge classes between named ports (precedes leaves next and arrives at previous). Nothing is drawn by side, and nothing depends on one particular edge being present: deleting an edge changes how the graph is drawn, not what it says.\n\n*Why:* Names say what a connection means; sides do not.\n\n*Checked by:* Test (mechanical).",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "canon-standard"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
