    {
      "id": "canon-standard-section-11",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "10. Events run through edges",
      "position": {
        "x": 2250,
        "y": 220
      },
      "width": 620,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "title": "10. Events run through edges",
        "body": "A Method runs only through an invokes edge from an event port to a Method in the same graph. There are no Event Handler nodes.\n\n*Why:* One model for events; this is already the rule everywhere.\n\n*Checked by:* The validator (mechanical).",
